# eBay plugin — its own environment. Copy this file and fill in the two
# values; the copy is gitignored.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# That is for a local run. In a RetroWatchdog deployment the same content goes
# in `.env.ebay` beside the app's `.env`, which compose reads with
# `required: false`.
#
# Secrets live in the plugin and never in the app: the app's manifest read
# learns only the NAMES of what a plugin needs, never a value. Register an
# application on developer.ebay.com (Browse API, client credentials) to get
# these two.

# eBay Browse API OAuth client credentials.
# The plugin exchanges these for an application token itself; the app never sees
# either value, and `GET /health` reports only whether BOTH are present, as a
# boolean `configured`. It never echoes them back.
EBAY_CLIENT_ID=
EBAY_CLIENT_SECRET=

# The port the plugin listens on INSIDE its container. It publishes no host
# port: only the app reaches it, over the compose network.
# PORT=8000

# Which of the five markets this process declares and serves, comma-separated
# ids. Unset means all five: ebay_uk, ebay_de, ebay_es, ebay_fr, ebay_us.
# EBAY_PLUGIN_MARKETS=ebay_uk,ebay_de

# Ceiling on the time one /search may spend, in milliseconds, and the budget
# used when a request names none. Matches the app's own 8000 ms fetch budget.
# EBAY_SEARCH_BUDGET_MS=8000
